///1MAC
Help by Willem Aandewiel
MAC - Digital Research macro assembler

///2SYNTAX
  E>A:MAC DEMO

MAC reads DEMO.ASM and normally creates DEMO.HEX, DEMO.PRN
and DEMO.SYM.

///2EXAMPLE
  E>A:MAC DEMO
  E>TYPE DEMO.PRN
  E>A:LOAD DEMO

Check the listing before converting HEX output into a COM file.

///2MACROS
MAC supports macro definitions and macro calls.
MACLIB can include external macro source from a .LIB file.
A text macro library is different from a .REL object library.

///2COMPARISON
ASM is the basic assembler. MAC produces absolute HEX output.
RMAC produces relocatable REL modules for LINK.
This page describes Digital Research MAC, not Microsoft M80.
